{"strongs": "H5677", "word": "עֵ֫בֶר", "translit": "e.ver", "root": "עבר", "morph": "N:N-M-P", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "Eber", "definition": "II. עֵ֫בֶר proper name, masculine Eber (perhaps eponym of Hebrews , form inferred from עִבְרִי , compare references there); — 1. 'son' of Shelah, and 'grandson' of Arpachshad Gen 10:24 ( J ) = 1Chr 1:18 ; Gen 11:14 ; Gen 11:15 ( P ); 'father' of Peleg and Joktan Gen 10:25 ( J ; with especially reference to Joktan v Gen 10:26 ff., i.e. to Arabians) = 1Chr 1:19 (compare v 1Chr 1:20 ff.), of Peleg specifically Gen 11:16 ; Gen 11:17 ( P ; with especially reference to Abraham v Gen 11:26 f.) compare 1Chr 1:25 (see v 1Chr 1:27 f.); in Gen 10:21 ( J ) Shem is called אֲבִי כָּלבְּֿנֵיעֵֿבֶר ; ᵐ5 Εβερ . — ׳ ע Num 24:24 perhaps (si vera lectio) belongs not here ( = עִבְרִים Hebrews , ᵐ5 Ἐβραίους , so Thes ), but below I. עֵבֶר = the (land) beyond (the river), || אַשּׁוּר , so Di Kau . 2. a Gadite chief 1Chr 5:13 , ᵐ5 Ωβηδ , ᵐ5 L Εβερ . 3. Benjamite names: \\ \\ a. 1Chr 8:12 , ᵐ5 Ωβηδ , ᵐ5 L Αβερ . \\ \\ b. 1Chr 8:22 ( עֵבֶר van d. H. Ginsb ; עֶבֶד Baer ), ᵐ5 Ωβδη , A Ωβηδ , ᵐ5 L Αβερ . 4. a priest Neh 12:20 ᵐ5 L Αβεδ .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5767')\">BDB5767</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H5677')\">H5677</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5766')\">BDB5766</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB5768')\">BDB5768</entry></div><p> II. <bdbheb>עֵ֫בֶר</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine</b> <highlightword>Eber</highlightword> (perhaps eponym of <highlight>Hebrews</highlight>, form inferred from <bdbheb>עִבְרִי</bdbheb>, compare references there); — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> 'son' of Shelah, and 'grandson' of Arpachshad <ref ref=\"Gen 10:24\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(1,10,24)\">Gen 10:24</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>) = <ref ref=\"1Chr 1:18\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"